  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, OnTriggerEnter and friends will trigger collisions for some protected objects - notably, colliders on avatars, but there may be others as well. This is a common point of confusion as your UdonBehaviour may suddenly die when it tries to examine a collider, and you may have difficulty reproducing this (because your avatar doesn't have colliders or triggers on it).\nI suspect it's rare to actually need this functionality; while there may be specific use cases that need to detect colliders on avatars, or maybe the quick menu, but for the most part it's just a debugging rabbit hole for Udon beginners. As such, I suggest that Udon filter these events, and guarantee that OnTriggerEnter and friends only be invoked when the collider is not a protected object.\nIt may be necessary for compatibility to add a flag to retain the old behavior - but the presence of protected colliders is in any case subject to change as VRC's UI changes, or as a player changes avatars, and they can still be potentially found by performing sphere/raycasts, so there are workarounds available for weird usecases.",
